  "summary": "Space now toggles the spider between walking and paused. While paused, the legs and body freeze in their current pose, and the next Space press resumes the walk from that pose. The gait clock only advances while walking, so there is no jump on resume. `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { walking: boolean }` starts as `{ walking: true }` and updates on every toggle. Typecheck passes. I did not run it in a browser, so the Space key and the pause/resume behaviour are untested."
